# Guide

A guide divides a substantial subject into chapters with their own titles and durable routes. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/guide/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use a multi-part guide when sections answer different tasks or are useful independently. A companion installation guide might separate preparation, installation and verification. If readers need the whole procedure at once, prefer a detailed single page with a contents list.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep a consistent title and chapter navigation. Identify the current chapter without a self-link, and provide previous/next destinations with chapter names. A combined print view is useful only when it contains the whole guide. Maintain cross-chapter terminology and version requirements.

## Home Assistant boundary

A sequence of guide pages is not a wizard and must not silently save progress. Do not hide necessary prerequisites on a previous page that a direct visitor may never have seen. The examples navigate between actual sections rather than fictional URLs.

